uuid "621b8204-3932-59dd-b595-a75ccb8e4c23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174316 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186174317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174316 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186174318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174316 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186174319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174316 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186174320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174316 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186174321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174316 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174316 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174316 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4ade0158-e250-507f-8ba8-b8ce91c7595f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174317 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174317 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174317 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a29f6694-b246-58ac-95b0-e97d347fa504" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174318 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174318 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174318 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c177145-c596-5550-85fe-72abe7eab484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174319 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174319 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174319 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23f5dcf3-90cb-5a3b-8ef6-b484dbb6f0fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174320 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174320 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174320 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45e0fb01-a577-58a5-a35e-8d9dca6b101f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174321 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174321 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174321 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "58836941-ff16-5464-8fc4-580970987b77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175888 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9717" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175888 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/08/089aa0d861b267352f9e5d83f47a00d5fd330f0f280268783e5a8e88cf947a98.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above. According to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175888 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc4500bc-8992-5148-95eb-6f84ae2508cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175888 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(82,70)$. So, our actual value is $y=70$.\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=82$ has the $y$-coordinate $65$. So, our estimated value is\n\n$$\n\\widehat{y}=65\n$$\n\n![](images/99/99e3741f602802e636e2e49ef755954343079b8c0d98453dac9364ddc08ef16f.png)\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - y^(^) \\\\\n&= 70 - 65 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $5$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175889 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9718" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175889 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is\n$y=0.5x+7$.\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=6$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175889 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb2190d0-5150-53ff-b7ab-ed364611bc8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175889 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^(^) &= 0.5x + 7 \\\\\n&= 0.5(6) + 7 \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - y^(^) \\\\\n&= 12 - 10 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175890 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9719" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175890 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7c/7c7bf33ee8878c6dc8e33622a5abe79a068b483ed19c0e177ecea31ab34b8777.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y)$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. When $x=4$, the regression equation underestimates the value of $y$.\n2. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n3. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175890 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3b40900e-ca06-5951-8261-aa13d8f966ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175890 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n$\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}$\nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=4$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual} > \\textrm{Estimated}$, and therefore the model underestimates this data point.\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b02727029ed43c985da639287afa452cbe1985dc2bae8eaa4f16452ac4c01518.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186524960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186525051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186543587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining Residuals From a Graph" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176033 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176034 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176034 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176034 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176034 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing Residuals Using the Regression Line Equation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176034 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176034 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0286d36b-217f-52e4-8580-e031b6dea31e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176035 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176035 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176035 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176035 #edb/ref 1039 "Interpreting Residual Plots" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176035 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176035 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "aa97e57a-70d8-5708-8b7d-fa05604a3f88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176138 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176138 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176827 #edb/ref 17592186