edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543550 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543550 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/24/243a4212d1128a79203493bf672ad1c956fe0f48aad6abbb910de2861d99669c.png)\n\nA dog food company records data on the number of dogs $(x)$ sheltered at some kennels across the country and the corresponding amount of dog food $y$ (in kilograms) consumed in a month. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above. \n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted data point?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543550 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2848e9c-e485-5752-8daf-a5d57b496ccb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543550 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(10,175).$ So, our actual value is $y=175.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=10$ has the $y$-coordinate $200.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=200.$\n\n![](images/2c/2cd59a9ae9c7ad474a9d5a308d4b8f3c9b96be70acdf1e3613dfc4757ff01766.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =175-200 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $-25\\,kg.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543587 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186543361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543587 #edb/ref 1069 "q-134808" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543587 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543587 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/08/08ce939458d5c298805692df7d10bed2abdcf81ec874da3f61dbe15f59fc141a.png)\n\nA biologist records the heights $y$ (in meters) of several oak trees at certain times $x$ (in years) after they were planted. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.  \n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543587 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f1b17b2b-5f71-5d88-80f9-025ec7f6d205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543587 #edb/ref 1074 "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,6.5).$ So, our actual value is $y=6.5.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $5.5.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=5.5.$\n\n![](images/ee/eedd1cadb2ba49fb95f9e18f9bef365942e53521e6894a270c9a1e1474f3ed71.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =6.5-5.5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $1\\,\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543601 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186543618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543601 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "106ec1c5-5aeb-55e4-9a89-04cf9274a237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543601 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186543562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543618 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186543628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543618 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "328f4cd9-6f09-53f8-b7dd-274af5b0a028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543618 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186543587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543628 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "47edabd6-568a-5a2a-87d9-33d6db405e8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186543628 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186543550 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
